    "gold_solution": "```python\nfrom gurobipy import *\n\ndef solve_problem():\n    m = Model(\"Disaster_Response_Logistics\")\n    m.setParam(\"TimeLimit\", 300)  # Set time limit to 300 seconds\n\n    # Data\n    depots = list(range(3))  # D0..D2\n    units = list(range(4))  # U0..U3\n    supplies = list(range(2))  # S0..S1\n    days = list(range(1))  # Day0..Day0\n\n    demands = [[[40.0], [22.11]], [[17.34], [23.47]], [[14.71], [17.97]], [[12.24], [17.56]]]\n    depot_supplies = [[[25.6], [33.78]], [[24.0], [40.48]], [[41.77], [29.05]]]\n    transport_costs = [[4.73, 3.59, 3.8, 2.95], [1.23, 3.13, 3.91, 1.27], [3.27, 4.91, 2.96, 2.75]]\n    risk_costs = [[99.72, 84.61, 76.23, 50.38], [140.52, 82.16, 50.43, 199.71], [78.81, 77.99, 56.24, 126.92]]\n    supply_volumes = [0.74, 0.8]\n    penalty_costs = [84.72, 92.91]\n    vehicle_cost = 10.0\n    vehicle_capacity = 100.0\n    total_vehicles = 20\n\n    # Decision variables\n    # Flow_D{d}_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}: Amount of supply s from depot d to unit u on day t\n    flows = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                for s in supplies:\n                    flows[(d, u, s, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Flow_D{d}_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Slack_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}: Shortage of supply s at unit u on day t\n    slacks = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for u in units:\n            for s in supplies:\n                slacks[(u, s, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Slack_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Veh_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}: Number of vehicles on route d->u on day t\n    vehicles = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                vehicles[(d, u, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.INTEGER, name=f\"Veh_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Route_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}: Route d->u is active on day t (binary)\n    routes = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                routes[(d, u, t)] = m.addVar(vtype=GRB.BINARY, name=f\"Route_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Objective: Minimize total cost (transport + penalty + vehicle + risk)\n    obj = quicksum(\n        transport_costs[d][u] * flows[(d, u, s, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units for s in supplies\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        penalty_costs[s] * slacks[(u, s, t)]\n        for t in days for u in units for s in supplies\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        vehicle_cost * vehicles[(d, u, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        risk_costs[d][u] * routes[(d, u, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units\n    )\n    m.setObjective(obj, GRB.MINIMIZE)\n\n    # Depot capacity constraints: Total outflow <= supply\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for s in supplies:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(flows[(d, u, s, t)] for u in units) <= depot_supplies[d][s][t],\n                    name=f\"DepotCap_D{d}_S{s}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Demand constraints: Inflow + slack >= demand\n    for t in days:\n        for u in units:\n            for s in supplies:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(flows[(d, u, s, t)] for d in depots) + slacks[(u, s, t)] >= demands[u][s][t],\n                    name=f\"Demand_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Vehicle capacity constraints: Total volume <= vehicles * capacity\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(supply_volumes[s] * flows[(d, u, s, t)] for s in supplies) <= vehicle_capacity * vehicles[(d, u, t)],\n                    name=f\"VehCap_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Route activation constraints: vehicles <= total_vehicles * route\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    vehicles[(d, u, t)] <= total_vehicles * routes[(d, u, t)],\n                    name=f\"RouteAct_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Fleet size constraints: Total vehicles <= total_vehicles\n    for t in days:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(vehicles[(d, u, t)] for d in depots for u in units) <= total_vehicles,\n            name=f\"FleetSize_Day{t}\"\n        )\n\n    m.optimize()\n    return m\n```",
    "LLM_description": "Situation:\nA severe cyclone has disrupted road networks across Riverside Province. Key ground routes are intermittently passable due to debris, flooding, and security risks. Supply Depot Alpha (Portside), Supply Depot Bravo (Inland Rail Hub), and Supply Depot Charlie (Aerial Staging Area) have limited stocks of life-saving items (e.g., medical consumables and potable water). Forward Operating Base Falcon (northern foothills), Field Hospital Delta (urban center), IDP Camp Echo (coastal lowlands), and 3rd Relief Battalion Distribution Point Foxtrot (valley corridor) require immediate resupply. Movement along the eastern artery and valley approaches is high risk and may require route clearance and escorts. Bridge load limits and shifting landslides constrain convoy size and timing.\n\nMission:\nDeliver critical supplies from depots to the four supported units within the current operational period, maximizing life-saving effect while minimizing total operational cost (transport, shortage penalties, vehicle deployment, and fixed route security risk costs).\n\nExecution/Concept:\n- Supply and demand:\n  - Push direct shipments from each depot to supported units, not to exceed available stocks at each depot. Unmet demand, if any, will be captured as controlled shortfall and penalized.\n- Movement and capacity:\n  - Assign vehicles to depot\u2013unit routes. The total load per route will respect vehicle capacity limits; supply-specific volume factors will govern how much fits per vehicle.\n  - The fleet is finite and shared across all routes; total deployed vehicles cannot exceed the available fleet.\n- Costs and route activation:\n  - Transport costs apply per supply and route. Each deployed vehicle incurs a per-vehicle cost.\n  - Critically, activating any route (sending at least one vehicle on a specific depot\u2013unit corridor during the period) triggers a fixed Risk Cost representing security overhead (escort teams, route clearance, and monitoring). This cost is incurred once per active route regardless of the number of vehicles subsequently sent on that route.\n  - To control overhead, concentrate flows on fewer activated routes where feasible, balancing transport costs, risk exposure, and time.\n- Risk and access:\n  - Prioritize secure corridors and confirmed passable windows. High-risk corridors will only be activated if the life-saving benefit outweighs the fixed risk cost and transport expenditure.\n- Shortfalls and priorities:\n  - If demand cannot be fully met due to stock, access, or fleet constraints, allocate to the most critical needs first. Any shortfall will be minimized, given the penalty for unmet demand.\n\nAnnex A - Logistics Data:\nUnit Demands (Units x Supplies):\nUnit\\Supply | S 0 | S 1\n-----------------------\nU 0        |  40.00 |  22.11\nU 1        |  17.34 |  23.47\nU 2        |  14.71 |  17.97\nU 3        |  12.24 |  17.56\nDepot Supplies (Depots x Supplies):\nDepot\\Supply | S 0 | S 1\n------------------------\nD 0        |  25.60 |  33.78\nD 1        |  24.00 |  40.48\nD 2        |  41.77 |  29.05\nTransport Costs (Depot x Unit):\nDepot\\Unit | U 0 | U 1 | U 2 | U 3\n----------------------------------\nD 0        |   4.73 |   3.59 |   3.80 |   2.95\nD 1        |   1.23 |   3.13 |   3.91 |   1.27\nD 2        |   3.27 |   4.91 |   2.96 |   2.75\nRisk Costs (Depot x Unit):\nDepot\\Unit | U 0 | U 1 | U 2 | U 3\n----------------------------------\nD 0        |  99.72 |  84.61 |  76.23 |  50.38\nD 1        | 140.52 |  82.16 |  50.43 | 199.71\nD 2        |  78.81 |  77.99 |  56.24 | 126.92\nPenalty Costs per Unit Shortage: [Supply S0: 84.72, Supply S1: 92.91]\nVolume per Supply Unit: [Supply S0: 0.74, Supply S1: 0.8]\nFleet Parameters: Cost 10.0, Capacity 100.0, Total 20",
    "LLM_description_template": "Situation:\nA severe cyclone has disrupted road networks across Riverside Province. Key ground routes are intermittently passable due to debris, flooding, and security risks. Supply Depot Alpha (Portside), Supply Depot Bravo (Inland Rail Hub), and Supply Depot Charlie (Aerial Staging Area) have limited stocks of life-saving items (e.g., medical consumables and potable water). Forward Operating Base Falcon (northern foothills), Field Hospital Delta (urban center), IDP Camp Echo (coastal lowlands), and 3rd Relief Battalion Distribution Point Foxtrot (valley corridor) require immediate resupply. Movement along the eastern artery and valley approaches is high risk and may require route clearance and escorts. Bridge load limits and shifting landslides constrain convoy size and timing.\n\nMission:\nDeliver critical supplies from depots to the four supported units within the current operational period, maximizing life-saving effect while minimizing total operational cost (transport, shortage penalties, vehicle deployment, and fixed route security risk costs).\n\nExecution/Concept:\n- Supply and demand:\n  - Push direct shipments from each depot to supported units, not to exceed available stocks at each depot. Unmet demand, if any, will be captured as controlled shortfall and penalized.\n- Movement and capacity:\n  - Assign vehicles to depot\u2013unit routes. The total load per route will respect vehicle capacity limits; supply-specific volume factors will govern how much fits per vehicle.\n  - The fleet is finite and shared across all routes; total deployed vehicles cannot exceed the available fleet.\n- Costs and route activation:\n  - Transport costs apply per supply and route. Each deployed vehicle incurs a per-vehicle cost.\n  - Critically, activating any route (sending at least one vehicle on a specific depot\u2013unit corridor during the period) triggers a fixed Risk Cost representing security overhead (escort teams, route clearance, and monitoring). This cost is incurred once per active route regardless of the number of vehicles subsequently sent on that route.\n  - To control overhead, concentrate flows on fewer activated routes where feasible, balancing transport costs, risk exposure, and time.\n- Risk and access:\n  - Prioritize secure corridors and confirmed passable windows. High-risk corridors will only be activated if the life-saving benefit outweighs the fixed risk cost and transport expenditure.\n- Shortfalls and priorities:\n  - If demand cannot be fully met due to stock, access, or fleet constraints, allocate to the most critical needs first. Any shortfall will be minimized, given the penalty for unmet demand.\n\nAnnex A - Logistics Data:\n{DEMANDS}\n{DEPOT_SUPPLIES}\n{TRANSPORT_COSTS}\n{RISK_COSTS}\n{PENALTY_COSTS}\n{SUPPLY_VOLUMES}\nFleet Parameters: Cost {VEHICLE_COST}, Capacity {VEHICLE_CAPACITY}, Total {TOTAL_VEHICLES}"
